{"id": "EUVD-2026-83256", "enisaUuid": "fdf25f4c-6095-3697-938b-a6dc9eae7f49", "description": "uri-js through 4.4.1 contains an improper UTF-8 decoding vulnerability in pctDecChars() that decodes invalid and overlong percent-encoded sequences into ASCII metacharacters. Attackers can craft percent-encoded payloads to bypass platform decoder validation and inject path traversal or CRLF sequences that downstream consumers process without filtering.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T17:51:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:23:10", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js/issues/106", "https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js", "https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js/blob/a1acf730b4bba3f1097c9f52e7d9d3aba8cdcaae/src/uri.ts#L103-L141", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/uri-js-through-4.4.1-improper-utf-8-decoding-via-pctdecchars"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7g43-p94j-qr58", "CVE-2026-93751"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d01888b6-1b14-30e1-9264-3a435f6969ec", "product": {"name": "uri-js", "vendor": {"name": "garycourt"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.4.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b6929d26-7849-3e72-9b4e-e70db4def0e8", "vendor": {"name": "garycourt"}}], "isExploited": false}